  "title": "Answer: experience is something done, not a state",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "a10d8ac2-c7af-4f02-87ba-0961b191ec49",
      "text": "Experience is not a state or an occurrence in the mind or brain but a way of acting, and its qualitative features are aspects of that activity. Qualia, as intrinsic properties of experiential states, do not exist.",
